# The stern gallery at sundown (rooms/marrow_gallery.adv). Optional, no puzzle: Vane off duty, a
# glass poured for Pell, and the nearest she comes to a compliment. Each goodnight walks the two
# of them back into the cabin together, which is where she keeps until the fog.
dialogue gallery
  node root vane "Out here I'm off duty, clerk. I'm rude for pleasure, not for pay."
    > "Who's the other glass for?" if not seen:gallery.pell -> pell
    > "Why do you still sail, captain?" if not seen:gallery.why -> why
    > "There's a star out already." if not seen:gallery.liar -> liar
    > "Two out of three, captain." if quill_navigator and crew_agree and not seen:gallery.quill2 -> count
    > "Quill's taking sights with Pell's sextant." if quill_navigator and not crew_agree and not seen:gallery.quill2 -> quill
    > "Do you know what's in Cray's crates?" if kelp_seen and not seen:gallery.crates -> crates
    > "Goodnight, captain." if not seen:gallery.insult -> night
    > "Goodnight, captain." if seen:gallery.insult -> later
  # Out on the gallery again, after a first goodnight.
  node again vane "The sun doesn't set twice for anybody, clerk. Not even for customs."
    > "Who's the other glass for?" if not seen:gallery.pell -> pell
    > "Why do you still sail, captain?" if not seen:gallery.why -> why
    > "There's a star out already." if not seen:gallery.liar -> liar
    > "Two out of three, captain." if quill_navigator and crew_agree and not seen:gallery.quill2 -> count
    > "Quill's taking sights with Pell's sextant." if quill_navigator and not crew_agree and not seen:gallery.quill2 -> quill
    > "Do you know what's in Cray's crates?" if kelp_seen and not seen:gallery.crates -> crates
    > "Goodnight, captain." if not seen:gallery.insult -> night
    > "Goodnight, captain." if seen:gallery.insult -> later
  # Between subjects.
  node more narrator "Vane drinks. The sun goes down another inch."
    > "Who's the other glass for?" if not seen:gallery.pell -> pell
    > "Why do you still sail, captain?" if not seen:gallery.why -> why
    > "There's a star out already." if not seen:gallery.liar -> liar
    > "Two out of three, captain." if quill_navigator and crew_agree and not seen:gallery.quill2 -> count
    > "Quill's taking sights with Pell's sextant." if quill_navigator and not crew_agree and not seen:gallery.quill2 -> quill
    > "Do you know what's in Cray's crates?" if kelp_seen and not seen:gallery.crates -> crates
    > "Goodnight, captain." if not seen:gallery.insult -> night
    > "Goodnight, captain." if seen:gallery.insult -> later

  # Pell's glass. "You make me finish it for you" (vane.adv, at the log) is the other half.
  node pell vane "Pell's. Forty years, he'd start a sentence and I'd finish it for him. Usually wrong. It saved time."
    -> pell2
  node pell2 vane "Then last winter he stopped mid-sentence. I couldn't think how it ended. First time in forty years."
    > "What do you think he was going to say?" -> guess
    > "I have his log, captain." if has pell_log -> log
    > "(Say nothing.)" -> owed
  node guess vane "Something about the weather. Wrong, probably."
    -> owed
  node log vane "I know. I can see the corner of it from here. Inside, at the chart table. Out here is for rum."
    -> owed
  node owed narrator "She lifts the full glass, holds it over the wake, and sets it down again. Untouched."
    -> owed2
  node owed2 vane "The sea gets it at dark. Pell always said the sea was owed. I'd rather pay it in rum."
    note pell_glass "Captain Vane pours a glass of rum for Pell every sundown and gives it to the sea at dark. He always said the sea was owed. She'd rather pay it in rum."
    -> more

  # The letter under her pillow (marrow_cabin.adv, the bunk).
  node why vane "Ashore, people write you letters."
    > "You keep one in your novel. As a bookmark." if looked:marrow_cabin.bunk -> pillow
    > "And the sea doesn't?" -> sea
  node sea vane "The sea's never put a thing in writing. It does what it means, to your face. I find that restful."
    -> more
  node pillow vane "You've been under my pillow, clerk. …It keeps my place. Which is more than they ever did."
    > "Is it a good book?" -> book
  node book vane "A governess and a lighthouse keeper. Storms in every chapter. Nobody drowns. Most far-fetched thing I ever read."
    -> spine
  node spine narrator "By the state of the spine, she has read it four times."
    -> more

  # The night watch (watch.adv) teaches the Liar; the ending card brings it back.
  node liar vane "The Liar. First up, last down, and never where you left it. Pell named it."
    > "Quill's been teaching me. It moves." if night_watch -> honest
    > "Why the Liar?" if not night_watch -> honest
  node honest vane "Pell said it was the only honest star up there. All the others pretend they're standing still."
    -> more

  node count vane "I can count, clerk. A navigator and a crew in one day. First mates take a year to find the rum."
    -> quill2
  node quill vane "So I see. She's been sighting things all afternoon that don't need it. The sun twice. Hobb once."
    -> quill2
  node quill2 vane "Pell taught that girl every star there is, and never told her she was any good. That's my job now."
    > "Will you tell her?" -> tell
  node tell vane "I'll put it in the log. I'm told that's how things get true on this ship now."
    -> more

  # Cray's kelp (marrow_deck.adv, the crates). Act IV: "I didn't ask. That's worse, and cheaper."
  node crates vane "Cargo. I don't open cargo, clerk. I carry it. That's the whole art of chartering."
    > "I opened one." -> opened
  node opened vane "Then nail it shut again. He pays by the crate. I can't afford to know things by the crate."
    -> more

  node night vane "Clerk."
    -> turn
  node turn narrator "I turn round. She's still watching the wake."
    -> insult
  node insult vane "You came aboard a clerk, and you're still a clerk. I'm beginning to think it isn't the insult I meant."
    -> inside
  node inside narrator "She tips the full glass into the wake and goes in ahead of me. The sun finishes without her."
    go marrow_cabin
  node later vane "Go on in, clerk. I'll be at the chart table before you are. Captain's privilege."
    go marrow_cabin
